{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2271409","formula":"CaAl₃(SO₄)(PO₄)(OH)₆","hill":"Al3CaH6O14PS","elements":["H","O","Al","P","S","Ca"],"composition":{"H":6.0,"O":14.0,"P":1.0,"S":1.0,"Al":3.0,"Ca":1.0},"names":{"en":"Woodhouseite","ru":"Вудхаузеит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Woodhouseite belongs to the beudantite group AB3(XO4)(SO4)(OH)6 where A = Ba, Ca, Pb or Sr, B = Al or Fe and X = S, As or P. Minerals in this group are isostructural with each other and also with minerals in the crandallite and alunite groups. They crystallise in the rhombohedral system with space group R3m and crystals are usually either tabular {0001} or pseudo-cubic to pseudo-cuboctahedral. Woodhouseite was named after Professor Charles Douglas Woodhouse (1888–1975), an American mineralogist and mineral collector from the University of California, Santa Barbara, US, and one-time General Manager of Champion Sillimanite, Inc.","ru":"Вудхаузеит (англ. woodhouseite) — редкий минерал, гидроксилсульфатофосфат алюминия и кальция (двойная соль), из подгруппы бедантита группы алунита."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2271409","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodhouseite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%92%D1%83%D0%B4%D1%85%D0%B0%D1%83%D0%B7%D0%B5%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woodhouseite-113804.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q2668239","formula":"SrAl₃(SO₄)(PO₄)(OH)₆","names":{"en":"Svanbergite","ru":"Сванбергит","uk":"Сванбергіт"}